From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 20:46:42 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: read a linear image's input attachment through
 an array view

Android's swapchain offers VK_IMAGE_USAGE_INPUT_ATTACHMENT_BIT on every
surface, and Unity creates its swapchain with it: Angry Birds 2's images ask
for TRANSFER_SRC, TRANSFER_DST, COLOR_ATTACHMENT and INPUT_ATTACHMENT. Venus
imports each of those native buffers as a DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR image, and
this driver refused every one with VK_ERROR_INITIALIZATION_FAILED, so the
game never got a swapchain and its window stayed black.

The refusal came from how input attachments are bound, not from what Metal
can do. This driver reads every input attachment as a 2D array, and it made
that possible by creating the image itself as a 2D array texture. Metal makes
only a 2D texture of a buffer, so a linear layout could not be an input
attachment at all. But every colour attachment view already carries a 2D
array view of its image for input attachment reads, and Metal does make a 2D
array view of a 2D texture over a buffer; it reads back the same texels.

So a linear layout stays a 2D texture whatever its usage, and its input
attachment is read through that view -- including through a one-layer 2D
array view, whose own texture is still 2D. A modifier image, which already
renders, now offers the input attachment Vulkan requires of any format with
the colour attachment feature, and the image format query answers what
vkCreateImage accepts. Plain linear tiling keeps the capabilities it has
always had. Optimal images are unchanged.

The Meson suite pins the policy, and a new test creates a modifier image with
the swapchain's usage from both a modifier list and an explicit layout,
clears it, and reads the clear back through each view's input attachment
texture.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
